WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.700
Our heroes have witnessed Laverre City Gym Leader Valerie’s

2
00:00:07.766 --> 00:00:10.166
remarkable skills firsthand,

3
00:00:10.233 --> 00:00:15.033
and now it’s Ash’s turn to face this Fairy-type trainer in a Gym Battle.

4
00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:20.866
Ash’s sixth Kalos Gym Badge is on the line. What will his strategy be?

5
00:00:26.833 --> 00:00:29.866
- Yes! It’s finally today.
- Pika!

6
00:00:29.933 --> 00:00:33.900
Hey, Sawyer? Have you ever watched a Gym battle before?

7
00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:35.533
No. It’s my first time.

8
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.066
My heart's pounding like you wouldn't even believe.

9
00:00:38.133 --> 00:00:40.200
But Ash is battling, not you.

10
00:00:40.266 --> 00:00:42.300
I hope you'll be out there cheering.

11
00:00:42.366 --> 00:00:43.866
- Pika.
- Of course.

12
00:00:43.933 --> 00:00:47.266
Have you figured out how to deal with Valerie's Fairy types?

13
00:00:47.333 --> 00:00:51.300
Judging from her challenge yesterday, it's clear there's a lot we don't know

14
00:00:51.366 --> 00:00:54.200
- about her battling techniques.
- I haven't. Not yet.

15
00:00:54.266 --> 00:00:56.200
- Pika, pika.
- Will you be OK?

16
00:00:56.266 --> 00:01:00.133
Ash will be fine. Ash and his Pokémon have always worked together,

17
00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.600
which is the key to winning Gym Badges.

18
00:01:02.666 --> 00:01:07.300
- That's why he'll be able to beat Valerie.
- Yeah, you've got that right.

19
00:01:11.966 --> 00:01:13.766
♪ You're just a kid on a quest ♪

20
00:01:13.833 --> 00:01:15.533
♪ To be the best of the best ♪

21
00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:18.966
♪ Someday you're destined for power and glory ♪

22
00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:20.433
♪ You know you're up to the test ♪

23
00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:24.266
♪ There's only one way to tell this story ♪

24
00:01:24.333 --> 00:01:27.533
♪ Be a hero! Be a hero! ♪

25
00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.966
♪ All the power is at your command ♪

26
00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:34.933
♪ Face your fears and show you're a hero ♪

27
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:39.633
♪ The future of the world is in your hand! ♪

28
00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:41.900
♪ Pokémon! ♪

29
00:01:46.066 --> 00:01:48.733
Fairy-type Trickery!

30
00:01:57.566 --> 00:02:00.066
We welcome you to the Laverre Gym.

31
00:02:00.133 --> 00:02:02.166
I'm here for a Gym Battle.

32
00:02:25.266 --> 00:02:27.033
-Pika!

33
00:02:39.733 --> 00:02:41.700
Pika, pi.

34
00:02:46.433 --> 00:02:47.433
Hm.

35
00:02:49.466 --> 00:02:52.233
- Treecko.
- We're spectators today, OK?

36
00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:55.466
I know that if we watch their battle closely, we'll learn a lot.

37
00:02:55.533 --> 00:02:57.066
I'll be sure to make lots of notes

38
00:02:57.133 --> 00:02:58.666
- on this experience.
- Treecko.

39
00:02:58.733 --> 00:03:00.766
- All we will too.
- Right.

40
00:03:00.833 --> 00:03:02.766
All right! Learning's fun.

41
00:03:04.833 --> 00:03:08.933
- Hold on. Where's Valerie?
- No need to rush these things.

42
00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.633
The Gym Leader will be here shortly.

43
00:03:13.833 --> 00:03:16.133
Whoa.

44
00:03:18.966 --> 00:03:20.066
Huh?

45
00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:27.766
Like a designer's Gym should look.

46
00:03:30.833 --> 00:03:32.566
- It's her.
- Pika.

47
00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:35.133
It's Valerie.

48
00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.333
The time has finally come.

49
00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:45.233
Valerie, the Laverre Gym Leader, is now making her entrance.

50
00:03:48.866 --> 00:03:51.733
I welcome you all to my Gym.

51
00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:56.366
I believe your name is Ash, right? How many Gym Badges do you have?

52
00:03:56.433 --> 00:04:01.433
I have five of them right now. And after this, I'll have six Gym Badges.

53
00:04:03.233 --> 00:04:07.266
Such spirit. You're certainly confident, aren't you?

54
00:04:07.333 --> 00:04:09.666
But I won't let you win that easily.

55
00:04:09.733 --> 00:04:11.866
The stronger the opponents we face,

56
00:04:11.933 --> 00:04:14.533
the more we get totally fired up and psyched.

57
00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:17.266
We're not gonna lose this battle, no way.

58
00:04:17.333 --> 00:04:20.266
All right, then. Shall we?

59
00:04:20.333 --> 00:04:24.133
The Laverre Gym Battle between Valerie, the Gym Leader,

60
00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:28.266
and Ash from Pallet Town, the challenger, will now get underway.

61
00:04:29.433 --> 00:04:31.866
Each trainer will have the use of two Pokémon,

62
00:04:31.933 --> 00:04:37.366
and the battle will be over when either trainer's Pokémon are unable to continue.

63
00:04:37.433 --> 00:04:41.600
Furthermore, only the challenger will be permitted to substitute Pokémon.

64
00:04:41.666 --> 00:04:42.966
That's all.

65
00:04:43.033 --> 00:04:45.133
- Two, huh?
- Pikachu.

66
00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.900
- Huh?
- I'll choose first.

67
00:04:46.966 --> 00:04:48.366
Huh?

68
00:04:49.233 --> 00:04:50.533
Sylveon...

69
00:04:51.366 --> 00:04:52.700
appear.

70
00:04:55.266 --> 00:04:57.400
Sylveon!

71
00:04:57.466 --> 00:04:58.633
It's Sylveon.

72
00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:01.666
- Sylve, syl, sylv.
- Veon!

73
00:05:01.733 --> 00:05:02.933
Veon, syl, sylv.

74
00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:06.300
- Pika...
- It's just like Serena said.

75
00:05:06.366 --> 00:05:08.133
Valerie talks with Pokémon.

76
00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.433
Hm?

77
00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:13.933
Honestly? I've always wanted to be a Pokémon,

78
00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.366
so I managed to learn how to speak with them.

79
00:05:16.433 --> 00:05:17.733
Awesome.

80
00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:20.933
It's true I can't communicate with every Pokémon,

81
00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:24.466
but I can understand most of what my Pokémon are telling me.

82
00:05:24.533 --> 00:05:28.133
She learned how to talk to Pokémon because she wants to be a Pokémon?

83
00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:31.133
I use Fairy-type Pokémon in my gym.

84
00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:34.266
I happen to be quite strong, so watch your step.

85
00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:36.400
Veon.

86
00:05:36.466 --> 00:05:41.000
Here's my first Pokémon. Fletchinder, I choose you.

87
00:05:41.066 --> 00:05:43.166
Fletch!

88
00:05:46.466 --> 00:05:49.666
- Pika, pika!
- Good. Well, then, make your move.

89
00:05:49.733 --> 00:05:51.833
- 'Kay, here we go.
- Treecko.

90
00:05:54.166 --> 00:05:56.600
Battle begin!

91
00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:01.500
Let's do this, Fletchinder! Now, use Steel Wing!

92
00:06:01.566 --> 00:06:03.733
Fletchinder!

93
00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:08.433
- Wow, that was perfect.
- And it was super effective.

94
00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:11.133
Got it. That just showed us Steel-type moves

95
00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:13.800
are really effective against Fairy-type Pokémon.

96
00:06:13.866 --> 00:06:16.433
Huh? Are you all right?

97
00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:18.833
- Veon.
- All right.

98
00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:23.433
We can't underestimate them, can we? But this time, it's our turn.

99
00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:24.433
Disarming Voice!

100
00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:27.033
Veon!

101
00:06:27.833 --> 00:06:29.266
Fle...

102
00:06:29.333 --> 00:06:31.633
Now, Fletchinder. Use Peck, let's go!

103
00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:35.166
Fletchinder!

104
00:06:35.233 --> 00:06:36.400
Quick, catch it.

105
00:06:36.466 --> 00:06:38.400
Fletchinder!

106
00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:41.000
- No way!
- Pika!

107
00:06:41.133 --> 00:06:44.433
Sylve-ee-ee-ee!

108
00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:47.700
- Oh, no!
- What a weird way to battle.

109
00:06:47.766 --> 00:06:51.233
A Pokémon battle isn't just about an exchange of moves.

110
00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:54.233
Some trainers know everything about their Pokémon's skills

111
00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:56.433
and will use them to their full potential.

112
00:06:56.500 --> 00:06:59.433
- Valerie's exceptionally good at that.
- Ee-ee-ee!

113
00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:02.566
- All right!
- You can do it, Sylveon.

114
00:07:02.633 --> 00:07:05.633
- Go all the way!
- We're not done just yet.

115
00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:07.200
Sylveon, Fairy Wind.

116
00:07:07.266 --> 00:07:10.166
Veon!

117
00:07:10.233 --> 00:07:15.000
Fletch! Fletch! Fletch!

118
00:07:15.066 --> 00:07:16.533
- Ah!
- Pikachu!

119
00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:19.433
- Incredible power.
- Fletchinder!

120
00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:22.300
- Denne-ne!
- Fletchinder, be strong.

121
00:07:24.333 --> 00:07:26.500
We need to untie those ribbons.

122
00:07:26.566 --> 00:07:28.566
So, what do you think, Ash?

123
00:07:28.633 --> 00:07:32.500
Sylveon's ribbons can do more than just flutter beautifully, you see.

124
00:07:32.566 --> 00:07:37.466
While Fairy types are graceful, they also possess dangerous hidden fangs.

125
00:07:38.633 --> 00:07:40.500
What's Ash going to do?

126
00:07:40.566 --> 00:07:43.400
Come on, Ash. Fletchinder, you can do it.

127
00:07:46.966 --> 00:07:50.233
Fletch! Fletch! Fletchinder!

128
00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:51.333
Valerie!

129
00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:54.100
When it comes to hidden fangs, Fletchinder has them too.

130
00:07:54.166 --> 00:07:55.366
Huh?

131
00:07:55.433 --> 00:07:59.166
Heat up, Fletchinder. And use Flame Charge.

132
00:07:59.233 --> 00:08:01.933
Fletchinder!

133
00:08:02.833 --> 00:08:04.333
Fletchinder!

134
00:08:07.366 --> 00:08:11.933
I'm impressed. Giga Impact.

135
00:08:13.866 --> 00:08:17.300
We won't back down. Use Steel Wing.

136
00:08:17.366 --> 00:08:19.100
Fletchinder!

137
00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:27.300
Fletchinder! Fletch!

138
00:08:28.833 --> 00:08:31.766
Sylveon!

139
00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:39.466
- Kali? Make the call.
- Uh, right.

140
00:08:39.533 --> 00:08:43.966
Sylveon is unable to battle. Fletchinder wins.

141
00:08:44.033 --> 00:08:47.666
- Yes. That's one down.
- Wow, you did it, Fletchinder.

142
00:08:47.733 --> 00:08:49.066
That was so cool.

143
00:08:49.133 --> 00:08:53.800
So that proves Steel-type moves are super effective on Fairy-type Pokémon.

144
00:08:53.866 --> 00:08:56.166
- Just like it's supposed to be.
- Treecko, Tree.

145
00:08:56.233 --> 00:09:00.233
Sylveon? Return, please.

146
00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:04.100
You battled wonderfully. Take a nice rest.

147
00:09:04.166 --> 00:09:07.466
Fletchinder hung in there and beat her first Pokémon.

148
00:09:07.533 --> 00:09:09.866
Hm. But I wonder what her next one is?

149
00:09:09.933 --> 00:09:13.466
She's a Gym Leader. Ash still can't let his guard down.

150
00:09:13.533 --> 00:09:15.833
There's still a very tough battle ahead.

151
00:09:18.133 --> 00:09:21.466
Be warned. It won't be the same this time.

152
00:09:23.566 --> 00:09:25.033
Spritzee.

153
00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:27.866
- There's that Spritzee.
- Spritzee.

154
00:09:27.933 --> 00:09:30.866
- Spritz, Spritzee.
- Spritz, Spritzee!

155
00:09:30.933 --> 00:09:32.366
Pika.

156
00:09:32.433 --> 00:09:34.766
We saw Spritzee's Dazzling Gleam yesterday,

157
00:09:34.833 --> 00:09:37.233
but we still don't know about its other moves.

158
00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:38.466
Hm.

159
00:09:38.533 --> 00:09:43.733
- Are you ready, Ash? It's your move again!
- You heard her!

160
00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:45.466
Fletchinder, let's go.

161
00:09:45.533 --> 00:09:47.800
- Fletch!
- Fletchinder, use Steel Wing!

162
00:09:47.866 --> 00:09:50.200
Fletchinder!

163
00:09:50.266 --> 00:09:52.800
- Spritzee!
- Now use Trick Room.

164
00:09:52.866 --> 00:09:54.533
Spritz, Spritzee!

165
00:10:07.733 --> 00:10:09.400
Trick Room, whoa.

166
00:10:13.966 --> 00:10:16.766
Who's that Pokémon?

167
00:10:20.966 --> 00:10:23.866
It's Mr. Mime!

168
00:10:23.933 --> 00:10:25.733
Mime.

169
00:10:26.966 --> 00:10:29.400
Fletchinder!

170
00:10:29.466 --> 00:10:31.000
Fletchinder!

171
00:10:31.066 --> 00:10:32.300
Fletchin! Fletchin!

172
00:10:32.366 --> 00:10:33.833
- Calm down.
- Fletchinder!

173
00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:35.833
You've gotta stay cool, OK?

174
00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:38.833
Surprised you, didn't we?

175
00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:42.866
- Valerie's using Trick Room.
- And if so, that can only mean one thing.

176
00:10:42.933 --> 00:10:45.466
Valerie's totally serious about this battle.

177
00:10:45.533 --> 00:10:47.000
I've never seen it before.

178
00:10:47.066 --> 00:10:49.066
So this is what they call Trick Room.

179
00:10:49.133 --> 00:10:51.533
-Is this a Fairy-type move?

180
00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:55.433
It's a Psychic-type move. And it's quite a troublesome one at that.

181
00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:57.366
Pika, pika.

182
00:10:57.433 --> 00:11:00.800
OK, Fletchinder, speed it up. Now use Flame Charge.

183
00:11:00.866 --> 00:11:01.900
Fletch!

184
00:11:01.966 --> 00:11:03.566
- Ash, no!
- Huh?

185
00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:06.233
Fletchinder!

186
00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:08.133
Hey, what's going on? -Chinder!

187
00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:10.133
It's not going any faster.

188
00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:14.366
Normally, Flame Charge is a move that will increase its user's speed.

189
00:11:14.433 --> 00:11:17.233
But the challenge is, when Trick Room is being used,

190
00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:20.833
the faster a Pokémon goes, the slower it actually is.

191
00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:24.233
So Ash called it not knowing that?

192
00:11:24.300 --> 00:11:27.566
- What are they gonna do now?
- It's dodging everything.

193
00:11:27.633 --> 00:11:30.166
Trick Room creates a mysterious space.

194
00:11:30.233 --> 00:11:33.066
So even though Spritzee's normally slower than Fletchinder,

195
00:11:33.133 --> 00:11:35.933
does it turn into the faster Pokémon in Trick Room?

196
00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:38.433
That's right.

197
00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:40.733
One more time. Use Flame Charge!

198
00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:44.000
Fletchinder! Fletch!

199
00:11:44.066 --> 00:11:45.600
Use Dazzling Gleam.

200
00:11:45.666 --> 00:11:49.033
Spritzee!

201
00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:51.500
Fletchinder!

202
00:11:51.566 --> 00:11:55.566
- Fletchinder, no!
- Well, well. Finished already?

203
00:11:55.633 --> 00:11:58.900
- Use Flame Charge.
- Again?

204
00:11:58.966 --> 00:12:01.033
Fletchinder!

205
00:12:01.100 --> 00:12:02.433
Fletch!

206
00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:05.433
- Gyro Ball.
- Spritzee!

207
00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:08.433
We're not done yet. Flame Charge!

208
00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:11.700
- Fletchinder! Fletchinder!
- Spritzee!

209
00:12:13.266 --> 00:12:15.800
What in the world could Ash be thinking?

210
00:12:15.866 --> 00:12:18.066
I'll bet you that he's got a strategy.

211
00:12:18.133 --> 00:12:19.033
Huh?

212
00:12:19.100 --> 00:12:20.100
Fletch...

213
00:12:20.166 --> 00:12:23.333
- I know you can do it. Hang in there.
- Fletchinder!

214
00:12:23.400 --> 00:12:26.700
Do your best and keep using Flame Charge, go!

215
00:12:26.766 --> 00:12:29.266
I wonder what trick he's got up his sleeve.

216
00:12:29.333 --> 00:12:30.600
Use Dazzling Gleam.

217
00:12:31.500 --> 00:12:33.800
Chinder! Fletchinder!

218
00:12:33.866 --> 00:12:35.533
Spritzee!

219
00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:38.466
It's like Fletchinder's getting slower on purpose.

220
00:12:38.600 --> 00:12:42.000
- Spritzee!
- Fletchin!

221
00:12:42.066 --> 00:12:46.000
Hang in there, Fletchinder. We'll get our chance.

222
00:12:48.333 --> 00:12:49.733
- Spritzee?
- Fletch?

223
00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:51.700
Dear. We're out of time.

224
00:12:52.766 --> 00:12:54.733
Fletchinder, use Steel Wing.

225
00:12:54.800 --> 00:12:56.466
Chinder! Fletchinder!

226
00:12:56.533 --> 00:13:00.100
Of course. Now I understand what Ash is up to.

227
00:13:00.166 --> 00:13:03.533
He kept on using Flame Charge so Fletchinder could attack at high speed

228
00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:05.433
as soon as Trick Room disappeared.

229
00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:07.133
- Ash planned it?
- All right.

230
00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:09.833
- Not so fast.
- Huh?

231
00:13:09.900 --> 00:13:12.166
Moonblast.

232
00:13:15.300 --> 00:13:18.566
Spritzee!

233
00:13:18.633 --> 00:13:20.300
Chinder!

234
00:13:21.633 --> 00:13:23.066
- Fletchinder, no!
- Pika.

235
00:13:23.133 --> 00:13:25.066
Fletchinder...

236
00:13:25.133 --> 00:13:29.300
Fletchinder is unable to battle. The winner is Spritzee.

237
00:13:29.366 --> 00:13:30.566
Yay!

238
00:13:30.633 --> 00:13:32.933
- Pika, pika.
- Argh!

239
00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:38.966
Thank you. But I must say, your multiple Flame Charges were a good idea.

240
00:13:39.033 --> 00:13:42.400
It's been a while since I've been surprised like that.

241
00:13:42.466 --> 00:13:46.566
That Moonblast, that was another dangerous hidden fang.

242
00:13:46.633 --> 00:13:48.333
Ash took much too long.

243
00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:50.900
And he paid a heavy price for doing that.

244
00:13:50.966 --> 00:13:55.000
Fletchinder, return. Get lots of rest.

245
00:13:55.066 --> 00:13:58.233
So how is Ash going to win this, huh?

246
00:13:58.300 --> 00:14:00.966
- Hm...
- Pika, pi.

247
00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:03.866
Hawlucha. I choose you.

248
00:14:05.500 --> 00:14:07.433
Ha-cha!

249
00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:10.800
Ha! Lu! Ha! Ha!

250
00:14:10.866 --> 00:14:13.666
My, my. Quite an amusing Pokémon.

251
00:14:13.733 --> 00:14:16.566
'Kay, Hawlucha's a Fighting and Flying type.

252
00:14:16.633 --> 00:14:20.033
But Fighting-type moves aren't very effective on Spritzee.

253
00:14:20.100 --> 00:14:25.033
- Ash chose Hawlucha anyway.
- Let's see what strategy Ash has in mind.

254
00:14:25.100 --> 00:14:28.766
- You can do it, Hawlucha!
- Hawlucha! Cha!

255
00:14:28.833 --> 00:14:31.266
Spritzee, Spritzee!

256
00:14:31.333 --> 00:14:33.700
- I'm counting on you, OK?
- Chalu.

257
00:14:33.766 --> 00:14:35.633
Now use Karate Chop.

258
00:14:37.766 --> 00:14:39.133
Ha!

259
00:14:39.200 --> 00:14:40.566
Use Trick Room.

260
00:14:40.700 --> 00:14:42.633
Hawlu! Huh?

261
00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:46.233
Spritzee!

262
00:14:46.300 --> 00:14:48.733
- Huh? They're using it again?
- Treecko!

263
00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:51.300
Cha?

264
00:14:51.366 --> 00:14:54.200
- Cha? Ha?
- Hawlucha!

265
00:14:54.266 --> 00:14:56.866
- Ha?
- Just relax. This is the ring for today.

266
00:14:58.033 --> 00:14:59.466
Hawlu! Lucha!

267
00:15:00.100 --> 00:15:04.233
Looks like somebody's having fun. We want you to enjoy yourselves.

268
00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:07.666
- Use Moonblast.
- Spritzee!

269
00:15:07.733 --> 00:15:09.666
Cha! Oof!

270
00:15:10.533 --> 00:15:12.466
Ha.

271
00:15:12.533 --> 00:15:14.466
-Pika!

272
00:15:14.533 --> 00:15:16.966
- Spritzee! Spritzee!
- What power.

273
00:15:18.566 --> 00:15:20.833
Ha, cha! Hawlucha.

274
00:15:20.900 --> 00:15:22.933
Yup. It's strong.

275
00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:27.166
My. You can talk to your Pokémon too, right?

276
00:15:27.233 --> 00:15:31.066
Not really talking. It's more like I can sense what they mean.

277
00:15:31.133 --> 00:15:32.900
I just kind of know.

278
00:15:32.966 --> 00:15:34.533
- Pika, pika.
- Ha-cha.

279
00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:36.766
You have much promise.

280
00:15:38.033 --> 00:15:40.133
Hawlucha, use X-Scissor.

281
00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:41.633
Ha-cha!

282
00:15:43.100 --> 00:15:45.600
- Huh?
- What did he do that for?

283
00:15:45.666 --> 00:15:49.133
Of course Bug-type moves are not very effective against Spritzee.

284
00:15:50.333 --> 00:15:51.600
Cha!

285
00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:56.233
- Huh?
- There he goes.

286
00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:58.733
I can tell Ash is up to something again.

287
00:15:58.800 --> 00:16:02.766
Hawlucha. Taking your opponent's moves head-on is your battling style.

288
00:16:02.833 --> 00:16:06.000
Watch Spritzee closely, and stay on its tail.

289
00:16:06.066 --> 00:16:08.433
- Spritzee! Spritzee! Spritzee! Spritzee!
- Hah.

290
00:16:08.500 --> 00:16:10.733
- He's such an interesting boy.
- Spritzee!

291
00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:12.666
So let's see what he's planning.

292
00:16:12.733 --> 00:16:15.933
Use Gyro Ball. Spritzee!

293
00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:17.433
Hawlucha, catch that.

294
00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:20.833
- Oof!
- Oh?

295
00:16:21.833 --> 00:16:25.200
All right. Hawlucha, use that speed.

296
00:16:25.700 --> 00:16:28.066
- Lucha, ha!
- Oh!

297
00:16:28.133 --> 00:16:30.233
- Wow.
- Hawlucha's using the spin

298
00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:31.300
from the Gyro Ball.

299
00:16:31.366 --> 00:16:33.300
Talk about thinking on your feet.

300
00:16:33.366 --> 00:16:36.933
- Very nice.
- Spin, Hawlucha. Use X-Scissor.

301
00:16:37.733 --> 00:16:39.000
Ha!

302
00:16:39.066 --> 00:16:42.133
Don't underestimate us! Dazzling Gleam!

303
00:16:43.733 --> 00:16:45.800
Cut right through that Dazzling Gleam.

304
00:16:45.866 --> 00:16:50.200
- Spritzee!
- Cha!

305
00:16:58.266 --> 00:17:00.200
- All right!
- Pika!

306
00:17:00.266 --> 00:17:03.933
Never seen that before. What an awesome X-Scissor.

307
00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:06.666
- They broke through...
- Trick Room.

308
00:17:06.733 --> 00:17:08.766
- Lucha.
- You did it, Hawlucha.

309
00:17:08.833 --> 00:17:09.900
Ha!

310
00:17:09.966 --> 00:17:11.766
Unbelievable.

311
00:17:11.833 --> 00:17:14.333
Even if a Bug-type move like X-Scissor

312
00:17:14.400 --> 00:17:16.133
isn't effective against a Fairy type,

313
00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:19.766
it is effective against Trick Room, which is a Psychic-type move.

314
00:17:19.833 --> 00:17:22.266
And that's the chance Ash took.

315
00:17:22.333 --> 00:17:26.066
- Ash is amazing.
- That's his battling style, all right.

316
00:17:26.133 --> 00:17:28.666
We never know what Ash is gonna come up with next.

317
00:17:28.733 --> 00:17:29.766
Denne-ne!

318
00:17:30.733 --> 00:17:33.366
I wonder if I can do that too?

319
00:17:33.433 --> 00:17:36.400
I wanted to destroy that Trick Room with X-Scissor.

320
00:17:36.466 --> 00:17:38.100
And that's just what I did.

321
00:17:38.166 --> 00:17:40.833
You're great at communicating with your Pokémon.

322
00:17:40.900 --> 00:17:42.900
You and Hawlucha are a perfect match.

323
00:17:43.033 --> 00:17:46.566
- Spritz. Spritzee.
- Spritzee. Let's do this.

324
00:17:46.633 --> 00:17:49.366
- OK. Now, use Flying Press.
- Cha! Ha!

325
00:17:49.433 --> 00:17:52.666
- Lucha!
- Spritzee.

326
00:17:52.733 --> 00:17:56.266
Spritzee, don't let it get too close. Moonblast.

327
00:17:56.333 --> 00:17:59.666
Spritzee!

328
00:17:59.733 --> 00:18:01.866
- Dodge it, quick!
- Ha!

329
00:18:02.900 --> 00:18:04.733
- Ha, ha, ha, ha!
- Now, High Jump Kick.

330
00:18:04.800 --> 00:18:06.700
Ha, ha, ha!

331
00:18:06.766 --> 00:18:08.200
Haaah!

332
00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:11.533
- Cha!
- Spritzee!

333
00:18:11.600 --> 00:18:14.333
Spritzee!

334
00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:15.866
Cha!

335
00:18:19.733 --> 00:18:21.300
Spritzee.

336
00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:28.233
Ah! Spritzee is unable to battle.

337
00:18:28.300 --> 00:18:32.966
Hawlucha is the winner. So the victor is Ash of Pallet Town.

338
00:18:33.033 --> 00:18:35.200
- All right!
- Pikachu!

339
00:18:37.833 --> 00:18:40.100
- Hawlucha, that was great.
- Pika, pika.

340
00:18:40.166 --> 00:18:44.100
- I just can't believe Valerie lost.
- I haven't seen that in so long.

341
00:18:47.200 --> 00:18:48.200
Spritzee?

342
00:18:48.266 --> 00:18:51.466
- Spritz, Spritzee?
- Spritzee.

343
00:18:51.533 --> 00:18:54.500
Spritz, Spritzee. You gave it your best effort.

344
00:18:54.566 --> 00:18:58.333
I'm so very proud of you, and Sylveon as well.

345
00:19:01.066 --> 00:19:06.366
That was truly well done. I haven't been that inspired in a while.

346
00:19:06.433 --> 00:19:07.933
Ash, you did it!

347
00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:09.466
Hawlucha. Great!

348
00:19:09.533 --> 00:19:13.666
What an amazing battle. I'll be sure to make a note of this experience.

349
00:19:13.733 --> 00:19:15.266
Treecko.

350
00:19:17.700 --> 00:19:20.633
Ash, you know how a trainer's heart becomes one

351
00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:24.633
with their Pokémon when they're backed into a corner during a battle.

352
00:19:24.700 --> 00:19:27.133
I'm wondering. Why is that?

353
00:19:27.200 --> 00:19:29.200
Heh. Hm.

354
00:19:29.266 --> 00:19:31.333
I'm not really sure.

355
00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:33.333
But I do know what you mean.

356
00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:40.300
Here's proof that you won at the Laverre Gym.

357
00:19:40.366 --> 00:19:42.500
I present you with the Fairy Badge.

358
00:19:42.566 --> 00:19:46.033
- Congratulations.
- Thank you very much.

359
00:19:49.100 --> 00:19:51.533
-Pika.

360
00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:53.333
We did it!

361
00:19:53.400 --> 00:19:57.033
- We got the Fairy Badge!
- Pi, Pikachu!

362
00:20:02.133 --> 00:20:03.866
That's wonderful, Ash.

363
00:20:03.933 --> 00:20:06.700
Fletchinder and Hawlucha battled really, really hard.

364
00:20:06.766 --> 00:20:09.666
And you also learned a brand-new battling strategy.

365
00:20:09.733 --> 00:20:13.366
- The Trick Room Breaker.
- Wow, Ash. You were so cool.

366
00:20:13.433 --> 00:20:15.600
I wanna be able to battle just like you.

367
00:20:15.666 --> 00:20:18.200
I've gotta know how you can battle like that.

368
00:20:18.266 --> 00:20:19.600
- You've gotta teach me!
- Pika.

369
00:20:19.666 --> 00:20:22.333
Uh... Not sure how to explain that...

370
00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:24.933
What are you thinking about when you're battling?

371
00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:27.266
Does Pikachu give you some kind of advice?

372
00:20:27.333 --> 00:20:29.500
It'll be easier to explain with a battle.

373
00:20:29.566 --> 00:20:30.933
- Yes!

374
00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:35.400
And so, Ash successfully overcame Spritzee's Trick Room,

375
00:20:35.466 --> 00:20:39.966
defeating Valerie at the Laverre City Gym and winning the Fairy Badge.

376
00:20:40.033 --> 00:20:42.800
Now, there are only two more badges to win

377
00:20:42.866 --> 00:20:45.666
before our hero gets to enter the Kalos League,

378
00:20:45.733 --> 00:20:48.900
as the journey continues.
